IMPORT prelude

-- Legislation Act 2003 (Commonwealth), Chapter 3 Part 3: repeal of spent legislative instruments, notifiable instruments and provisions (sections 48A to 48E).
-- Text: C2004A01224.txt, compilation C2019C00084; it is not the authorised text.
-- Same conventions as lga-register.l4: JUST TRUE (the text says yes), JUST FALSE (the text says no), NOTHING (the text does not say).
-- The day on which each repeal happens (subsections 48A(2), 48B(2), 48C(2) and 48D(2)) is computed in lga-time.l4.

§ `Section 48A: amending and repealing instruments`

-- "this section repeals a legislative instrument ... whose only legal effect is ...": a scope limit with no "only if", so an instrument outside it is NOTHING.
-- src:810 | (1) Subject to subsection (2), this section repeals a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument whose only legal effect is to amend or repeal one or more other legislative instruments or notifiable instruments, without making any application, saving or transitional provisions relating to the amendment or repeal.
@ref s 48A(1) (src:810-810)
GIVEN `it is a legislative instrument or a notifiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its only legal effect is to amend or repeal one or more other legislative instruments or notifiable instruments` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it makes an application, saving or transitional provision relating to the amendment or repeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48A(1): this section repeals the instrument` MEANS
    IF `it is a legislative instrument or a notifiable instrument`
       AND `its only legal effect is to amend or repeal one or more other legislative instruments or notifiable instruments`
       AND NOT `it makes an application, saving or transitional provision relating to the amendment or repeal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:811 | (1A) For the purposes of subsection (1), a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument is not taken to make an application, saving or transitional provision mentioned in that subsection merely because the instrument amends another such instrument to make an application, saving or transitional provision relating to the amendment or repeal.
@ref s 48A(1A) (src:811-811)
GIVEN `it amends another legislative instrument or notifiable instrument to make an application, saving or transitional provision relating to the amendment or repeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48A(1A): the instrument is taken to make an application, saving or transitional provision` MEANS
    IF `it amends another legislative instrument or notifiable instrument to make an application, saving or transitional provision relating to the amendment or repeal` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- "unless the instrument has been repealed earlier by subsection 38(3) or 42(1) or (2)": the earlier repeal answers JUST FALSE.
-- src:813 | (2) The repeal of the instrument by this section happens on the day after the latest of the following events occurs, unless the instrument has been repealed earlier by subsection 38(3) or 42(1) or (2):
-- src:814 | (aa) for a disallowable legislative instrument—the end of the last day on which the instrument or a provision of the instrument may be disallowed in a House of the Parliament;
-- src:815 | (a) for any legislative instrument or notifiable instrument—whichever of the following is applicable:
-- src:816 | (i) the commencement of the instrument, or of the last of its provisions to commence;
-- src:817 | (ii) if the last of its provisions that have not commenced are repealed, or cannot commence because of the occurrence of an event—that repeal, or the occurrence of that event;
-- src:818 | (b) for a legislative instrument to which section 42 does not apply or for a notifiable instrument—the registration of the instrument.
@ref s 48A(2) (src:813-818)
GIVEN `this section repeals the instrument under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument has been repealed earlier by subsection 38(3) or 42(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48A(2): the repeal by this section happens` MEANS
    IF `the instrument has been repealed earlier by subsection 38(3) or 42(1) or (2)` THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE (IF `this section repeals the instrument under subsection (1)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)

-- src:820 | (3) The repeal of the instrument by this section does not affect any amendment or repeal made by the instrument. This does not limit the effect of section 7 of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 as it applies in relation to the repeal of the instrument by this section because of section 13 of this Act.
@ref s 48A(3) (src:820-820)
GIVEN `the instrument is repealed by this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48A(3): the repeal affects any amendment or repeal made by the instrument` MEANS
    IF `the instrument is repealed by this section` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 48B: commencement instruments`

-- src:823 | (1) This section repeals a commencement instrument that provides for the commencement of one of the following (a primary law) or a provision (a primary provision) of one of the following:
-- src:824 | (a) an Act;
-- src:825 | (b) a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument.
@ref s 48B(1) (src:823-825)
GIVEN `it is a commencement instrument that provides for the commencement of an Act, or of a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument, or of a provision of one of them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48B(1): this section repeals the commencement instrument` MEANS
    IF `it is a commencement instrument that provides for the commencement of an Act, or of a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument, or of a provision of one of them` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:827 | (2) The repeal of the commencement instrument by this section happens on the day after the later of the following events occurs:
-- src:828 | (a) whichever of the following is applicable:
-- src:829 | (i) the commencement (or the last commencement) the commencement instrument provides for;
-- src:830 | (ii) if the commencement instrument provides for the commencement of a primary law, and the last of the provisions of the primary law that have not commenced are repealed—that repeal;
-- src:831 | (iii) if the commencement instrument provides for the commencement of a primary law, and the primary law (or the last of the provisions of the primary law) cannot commence because of the occurrence of an event—the occurrence of that event;
-- src:832 | (iv) if the commencement instrument provides for the commencement of a primary provision or primary provisions, and the primary provision (or the last of those primary provisions) is repealed, or cannot commence because of the occurrence of an event—that repeal, or the occurrence of that event;
-- src:833 | (b) the registration of the commencement instrument.
@ref s 48B(2) (src:827-833)
GIVEN `this section repeals the commencement instrument under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48B(2): the repeal by this section happens` MEANS
    IF `this section repeals the commencement instrument under subsection (1)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:835 | (3) The repeal of the instrument by this section does not affect any commencement the instrument provides for. This does not limit the effect of section 7 of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 as it applies in relation to the repeal of the instrument by this section because of section 13 of this Act.
@ref s 48B(3) (src:835-835)
GIVEN `the instrument is repealed by this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48B(3): the repeal affects any commencement the instrument provides for` MEANS
    IF `the instrument is repealed by this section` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 48C: amending and repealing provisions`

-- "this section repeals a provision ... if": the condition answers JUST FALSE when it fails.
-- src:838 | (1) Subject to subsection (2), this section repeals a provision of a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument if:
-- src:839 | (a) the instrument is not an instrument described in subsection 48A(1); and
-- src:840 | (b) the only legal effect of the provision (alone or in conjunction with other provisions of the instrument) is:
-- src:841 | (i) to amend or repeal one or more other legislative instruments or notifiable instruments; or
-- src:842 | (ii) to amend the instrument containing the provision.
@ref s 48C(1) (src:838-842)
GIVEN `it is a provision of a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is an instrument described in subsection 48A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only legal effect of the provision (alone or with other provisions of the instrument) is to amend or repeal one or more other legislative instruments or notifiable instruments` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only legal effect of the provision (alone or with other provisions of the instrument) is to amend the instrument containing the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48C(1): this section repeals the provision` MEANS
    IF NOT `it is a provision of a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE
        IF NOT `the instrument is an instrument described in subsection 48A(1)`
           AND (`the only legal effect of the provision (alone or with other provisions of the instrument) is to amend or repeal one or more other legislative instruments or notifiable instruments`
                OR `the only legal effect of the provision (alone or with other provisions of the instrument) is to amend the instrument containing the provision`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:844 | (2) The repeal of the provision by this section happens immediately after the latest of the following events occurs, unless the provision has been repealed earlier by subsection 38(3) or 42(1) or (2):
-- src:845 | (aa) if the provision is in a disallowable legislative instrument—the end of the last day on which the instrument or a provision of the instrument may be disallowed in a House of the Parliament;
-- src:846 | (a) if the provision is in any legislative instrument or notifiable instrument—whichever of the following is applicable:
-- src:847 | (i) the commencement of the provision;
-- src:848 | (ii) if the provision cannot commence because of the occurrence of an event—the occurrence of that event;
-- src:849 | (b) if the provision is in a legislative instrument to which section 42 does not apply or is in a notifiable instrument—the registration of the legislative instrument or notifiable instrument.
@ref s 48C(2) (src:844-849)
GIVEN `this section repeals the provision under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision has been repealed earlier by subsection 38(3) or 42(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48C(2): the repeal by this section happens` MEANS
    IF `the provision has been repealed earlier by subsection 38(3) or 42(1) or (2)` THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE (IF `this section repeals the provision under subsection (1)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)

-- src:851 | (3) The repeal of the provision by this section does not affect any amendment or repeal made by the provision. This does not limit the effect of section 7 of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 as it applies in relation to the repeal of the provision by this section because of section 13 of this Act.
@ref s 48C(3) (src:851-851)
GIVEN `the provision is repealed by this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48C(3): the repeal affects any amendment or repeal made by the provision` MEANS
    IF `the provision is repealed by this section` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- Subsection (5): "If subsection (1) repeals a provision ..., this section also repeals the following provisions".
-- src:853 | (5) If subsection (1) repeals a provision of a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument, this section also repeals the following provisions:
-- src:854 | (a) any other provision (for example, a Schedule) of the instrument that only identifies another instrument or provision that is amended or repealed;
-- src:855 | (b) any other provision (for example, a Part heading) of the instrument that only identifies (or groups) provisions that are amended or repealed.
-- src:856 | Note: See also subsection 45(2).
@ref s 48C(5) (src:853-856)
GIVEN `subsection (1) repeals a provision of the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other provision only identifies another instrument or provision that is amended or repealed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other provision only identifies (or groups) provisions that are amended or repealed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48C(5): this section also repeals the other provision` MEANS
    IF `subsection (1) repeals a provision of the instrument`
       AND (`the other provision only identifies another instrument or provision that is amended or repealed` OR `the other provision only identifies (or groups) provisions that are amended or repealed`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§ `Section 48D: commencement provisions`

-- src:859 | (1) Subject to subsection (2), this section repeals a provision (a commencement provision) of a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument, other than a commencement instrument, if the commencement provision provides solely for the commencement of one of the following (a primary law) or a provision (a primary provision) of one of the following:
-- src:860 | (a) the instrument;
-- src:861 | (b) an Act;
-- src:862 | (c) another instrument that is a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument.
@ref s 48D(1) (src:859-862)
GIVEN `it is a provision of a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument, other than a commencement instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision provides solely for the commencement of the instrument, an Act, or another legislative instrument or notifiable instrument, or of a provision of one of them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48D(1): this section repeals the commencement provision` MEANS
    IF NOT `it is a provision of a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument, other than a commencement instrument` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE
        IF `the provision provides solely for the commencement of the instrument, an Act, or another legislative instrument or notifiable instrument, or of a provision of one of them`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:864 | (2) The repeal of the commencement provision by this section happens immediately after the latest of the following events occurs, unless the commencement provision has been repealed earlier by subsection 38(3) or 42(1) or (2):
-- src:865 | (aa) if the commencement provision is in a disallowable legislative instrument—the end of the last day on which the instrument or a provision of the instrument may be disallowed in a House of the Parliament;
-- src:866 | (a) if the commencement provision is in any legislative instrument or notifiable instrument—whichever of the following is applicable:
-- src:867 | (i) the commencement (or the last commencement) the commencement provision provides for;
-- src:868 | (ii) if the commencement provision provides for the commencement of a primary law, and the last of the provisions of the primary law that have not commenced are repealed—that repeal;
-- src:869 | (iii) if the commencement provision provides for the commencement of a primary law, and the primary law (or the last of the provisions of the primary law) cannot commence because of the occurrence of an event—the occurrence of that event;
-- src:870 | (iv) if the commencement provision provides for the commencement of a primary provision, and the primary provision is repealed, or cannot commence because of the occurrence of an event—that repeal, or the occurrence of that event;
-- src:871 | (b) if the commencement provision is in a legislative instrument to which section 42 does not apply or is in a notifiable instrument—the registration of the legislative instrument or notifiable instrument.
@ref s 48D(2) (src:864-871)
GIVEN `this section repeals the commencement provision under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the commencement provision has been repealed earlier by subsection 38(3) or 42(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48D(2): the repeal by this section happens` MEANS
    IF `the commencement provision has been repealed earlier by subsection 38(3) or 42(1) or (2)` THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE (IF `this section repeals the commencement provision under subsection (1)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)

-- src:873 | (3) The repeal of the provision by this section does not affect any commencement the provision provides for. This does not limit the effect of section 7 of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 as it applies in relation to the repeal of the provision by this section because of section 13 of this Act.
@ref s 48D(3) (src:873-873)
GIVEN `the commencement provision is repealed by this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48D(3): the repeal affects any commencement the provision provides for` MEANS
    IF `the commencement provision is repealed by this section` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 48E: repeal by regulations`

-- jural: claim of nobody the text names | duty of the Attorney-General
-- src:877 | (2) Before the Governor-General makes a regulation for the purposes of subsection (1), the Attorney-General must be satisfied that the legislative instrument or notifiable instrument or provision to be repealed is spent or is no longer required.
@ref s 48E(2) (src:877-877)
GIVEN `a regulation is to be made for the purposes of subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48E(2): before the Governor-General makes the regulation the Attorney-General must be satisfied that the instrument or provision is spent or is no longer required` MEANS
    IF `a regulation is to be made for the purposes of subsection (1)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
